# Normalise to LF in the repo. Matters for the workflow: a CRLF-checked-out
# `run:` block breaks bash on the Linux runner (`sleep 123\r`).
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...but NOT the calendar. RFC 5545 mandates CRLF line endings, so this file
# must be stored and served byte-for-byte as generated. `-text` disables all
# EOL conversion; without it git would normalise it to LF and some calendar
# clients would reject the result.
*.ics -text
